From 0481e03a60f4216896e50f7b2ae95a31b03fd4f8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: dev <dev@localhost>
Date: Mon, 17 Aug 2026 00:22:02 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] N_eff: report, stop flagging on an uncalibrated threshold;
 exposure report

Measured on the fixture slate: N_eff saturates on SLATE SIZE, not lineup
count -- 7.2 at 20 lineups, 11.1 at 80, 11.8 at 150. The old floor
(0.2 * n_lineups) grows linearly, so above ~60 lineups it fired
unconditionally and carried no information. A random-selection baseline is
also not a threshold: selecting by expected score costs diversity against
random by construction (ratio saturates ~0.61), and that trade is the point.

So: report N_eff alongside the random-selection baseline at the same set
size, and flag only against a threshold the operator has calibrated
(neff_ratio or neff_floor). No default.

Exposure report: player exposures now carry position, team, salary,
projection, value (pts per $1k), ownership and team implied total, filterable
by position and sortable; new team exposure table with implied totals,
slots per lineup, and share of lineups containing the team.
